Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 15:25:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01023/11171] [outer-loop] Root-clutter prevention: sweeper +
 agent directives + make targets

Layered defense so root scratch stops accumulating (the .gitignore /*.py guard only
stops COMMITTING; agents still WRITE to root because the conductor launches every
subagent with cwd=PROJECT_ROOT):

- scripts/root_clutter_sweep.py: mechanical janitor. DRY-RUN by default; --apply
  quarantines untracked root *.py to .root-scratch-trash/<date>/ (reversible) and
  deletes regenerable build artifacts (main.*, vivado*, clockInfo.txt). Conservative:
  120-min age guard, allowlist of legit root files, NEVER touches tracked files.
- .gitignore: quarantine dir .root-scratch-trash/.
- Makefile: clean-scratch (dry-run) / clean-scratch-apply.
- AGENTS.md + GEMINI.md: directive to never write scratch to repo root.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
